
CS-1202 · Tuples & Sets
What We Learned From This Topic
🎯 Learning Outcomes
From Tuples & Sets, we learned that Python provides different containers for different engineering requirements. The correct container depends on whether we need order, mutability, or uniqueness.

1. 🔒 Tuples — Sealed Records
Tuples are created using round brackets ( ).

They are ordered.

They are immutable, so their elements cannot be changed after creation.

They are useful for fixed data such as specification limits and calibration constants.

SPEC = (24.95, 25.05)

lower, upper = SPEC

This is called tuple unpacking.


2. 🏷️ Sets — No-Duplicate Containers
Sets are created using { }.

They contain unique elements only.

Duplicate values are automatically removed.

They are useful for finding distinct values and performing fast membership checks.

codes = {"D01", "D07", "D01"}

Result:

{'D01', 'D07'}


